    "notes": "This is the primary multi-gate use case (SPEC.md §4.2.1): one gateway-scoped key, the same event observed once per gateway output (two calls with different outputReference) plus once at the gateway checkpoint (no options). All three MUST be sent as self-contained elements of one batch (SPEC.md §12.7), each carrying its own outputReference (or no key at all — '<absent>') and identical eventProperties. appVersion is resolved PER EVENT at enqueue and must survive batch serialization: the first element carries the per-event override '4.2.0' (originHint absent -> override), the second a literal JSON null (originHint present, no override), the third the constructor '1.0.0' (neither). An SDK that stamps the instance version on the whole batch at flush time fails this fixture. A server SDK has no deduplication, so nothing collapses. Batch element order is not asserted (unordered multiset)."
